# CHANGELOG.md is union-merged: when two branches each append a bullet under
# `## [Unreleased]`, git keeps both sides' lines instead of writing conflict
# markers (SCARIFW-1304). `union` is a built-in git merge driver, so there is no
# merge.*.driver config and nothing for a contributor to install.
#
# Accepted tradeoff: union merge is line-wise, so it can leave a duplicate or
# oddly-ordered bullet. Those are tidied when a release is cut.
CHANGELOG.md merge=union
